{"id":"CVE-2018-0500","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"debian","published":"2018-07-11T13:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T03:28:11.048Z","description":"Curl_smtp_escape_eob in lib/smtp.c in curl 7.54.1 to and including curl 7.60.0 has a heap-based buffer overflow that might be exploitable by an attacker who can control the data that curl transmits over SMTP with certain settings (i.e., use of a nonstandard --limit-rate argument or CURLOPT_BUFFERSIZE value).","cwe":["heap-based buffer overflow"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"curl before 7.61.0","versions":["affected curl before 7.61.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1041280","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1041280"},{"url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/ba1dbd78e5f1ed67c1b8d37ac89d90e5e330b628","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_2018-70a2.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201807-04","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201807-04"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2486","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2486"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3710-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3710-1"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-14618","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2018-09-05T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-04-15T20:54:19.698Z","description":"curl before version 7.61.1 is vulnerable to a buffer overrun in the NTLM authentication code. The internal function Curl_ntlm_core_mk_nt_hash multiplies the length of the password by two (SUM) to figure out how large temporary storage area to allocate from the heap. The length value is then subsequently used to iterate over the password and generate output into the allocated storage buffer. On systems with a 32 bit size_t, the math to calculate SUM triggers an integer overflow when the password length exceeds 2GB (2^31 bytes). This integer overflow usually causes a very small buffer to actually get allocated instead of the intended very huge one, making the use of that buffer end up in a heap buffer overflow. (This bug is almost identical to CVE-2017-8816.)","cwe":["CWE-131 CWE-131","CWE-122 CWE-122"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"[UNKNOWN]","product":"curl","versions":["affected 7.61.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/CVE-2018-14618.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201903-03","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201903-03"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3765-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3765-1"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3558","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3558"},{"url":"https://psirt.global.sonicwall.com/vuln-detail/SNWLID-2018-0014","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4286","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4286"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1041605","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1041605"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3765-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3765-2"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-14618","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/pdf/ssa-436177.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:1880","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:1880"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-16840","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2018-10-31T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-04-16T14:08:57.315Z","description":"A heap use-after-free flaw was found in curl versions from 7.59.0 through 7.61.1 in the code related to closing an easy handle. When closing and cleaning up an 'easy' handle in the `Curl_close()` function, the library code first frees a struct (without nulling the pointer) and might then subsequently erroneously write to a struct field within that already freed struct.","cwe":["CWE-416 CWE-416"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":4.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"The Curl Project","product":"curl","versions":["affected from 7.59.0 to 7.61.1"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201903-03","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201903-03"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-16840","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/81d135d67155c5295b1033679c606165d4e28f3f","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1042013","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1042013"},{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/CVE-2018-16840.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3805-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3805-1"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-16890","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2019-02-06T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-04-15T20:53:35.135Z","description":"libcurl versions from 7.36.0 to before 7.64.0 is vulnerable to a heap buffer out-of-bounds read. The function handling incoming NTLM type-2 messages (`lib/vauth/ntlm.c:ntlm_decode_type2_target`) does not validate incoming data correctly and is subject to an integer overflow vulnerability. Using that overflow, a malicious or broken NTLM server could trick libcurl to accept a bad length + offset combination that would lead to a buffer read out-of-bounds.","cwe":["CWE-125 CWE-125"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":5.4,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:L"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"The curl Project","product":"curl","versions":["affected 7.64.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2019/dsa-4386","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4386"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/106947","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"106947"},{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/CVE-2018-16890.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190315-0001/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3882-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3882-1"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2018-16890","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/8338a0f605bdbb3a6098bb76f666a95fc2b2f53f37fa1ecc89f1146f%40%3Cdevnull.infra.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[infra-devnull] 20190404 [GitHub] [incubator-openwhisk-runtime-ballerina] falkzoll commented on issue #15: Update to new base image jdk8u202-b08_openj9-0.12.1."},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/pdf/ssa-436177.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujul2019-5072835.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://support.f5.com/csp/article/K03314397?utm_source=f5support&amp%3Butm_medium=RSS","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:3701","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:3701"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1000005","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-01-24T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:33:49.200Z","description":"libcurl 7.49.0 to and including 7.57.0 contains an out bounds read in code handling HTTP/2 trailers. It was reported (https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/2231) that reading an HTTP/2 trailer could mess up future trailers since the stored size was one byte less than required. The problem is that the code that creates HTTP/1-like headers from the HTTP/2 trailer data once appended a string like `:` to the target buffer, while this was recently changed to `: ` (a space was added after the colon) but the following math wasn't updated correspondingly. When accessed, the data is read out of bounds and causes either a crash or that the (too large) data gets passed to client write. This could lead to a denial-of-service situation or an information disclosure if someone has a service that echoes back or uses the trailers for something.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1040273","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1040273"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3554-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3554-1"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4098","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4098"},{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_2018-824a.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/2231","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:1543","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:1543"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1000007","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-01-24T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:33:48.439Z","description":"libcurl 7.1 through 7.57.0 might accidentally leak authentication data to third parties. When asked to send custom headers in its HTTP requests, libcurl will send that set of headers first to the host in the initial URL but also, if asked to follow redirects and a 30X HTTP response code is returned, to the host mentioned in URL in the `Location:` response header value. Sending the same set of headers to subsequent hosts is in particular a problem for applications that pass on custom `Authorization:` headers, as this header often contains privacy sensitive information or data that could allow others to impersonate the libcurl-using client's request.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3554-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3554-2"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3554-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3554-1"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3558","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3558"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2018/dsa-4098","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-4098"},{"url":"https://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_2018-b3bf.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1040274","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1040274"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3157","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3157"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2018/01/msg00038.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20180129 [SECURITY] [DLA 1263-1] curl security update"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHBA-2019:0327","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHBA-2019:0327"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2019:1543","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2019:1543"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2019-5072832.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2020:0544","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2020:0544"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2020:0594","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2020:0594"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2022/04/27/4","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20220427 [SECURITY ADVISORY] curl auth/cookie leak on redirect"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
